WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.770
Certificate power is granted
in four separate places:

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:09.225
the old authority's own permissions, Intune,
Entra ID, and the lifecycle platform.

3
00:00:09.225 --> 00:00:11.037
That's where hidden risk sits.

4
00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:14.912
Several everyday console clicks
are really risk decisions.

5
00:00:14.912 --> 00:00:17.300
Leaving a template published just in case.

6
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.133
Trusting an authority in Entra
without a revocation list,

7
00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:23.688
so revoked certificates still sign in.

8
00:00:23.688 --> 00:00:25.800
Leaving bindings at the weak default.

9
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.158
And the platform's own account can approve

10
00:00:28.158 --> 00:00:30.650
certificates for every
template it reaches.

11
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.396
The decision for the CISO: map
every team in all four systems,

12
00:00:34.396 --> 00:00:37.843
keep privileged roles eligible
rather than permanent,

13
00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:42.338
and make sure no one can both change
and approve what an authority issues.

14
00:00:42.338 --> 00:00:44.040
Then the migration itself.
